---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const faqs = [["Why do I receive multiple reports per day?", "Each mailbox provider (Gmail, Microsoft, Yahoo) sends its own report. If mail claiming to be from your domain passed through multiple providers, you receive one report from each."], ["What should I do with unknown source IPs?", "Check if the IP belongs to a service you use. If not, it may be a spoofing attempt. If your policy is p=none, the mail was delivered but flagged in the report."]];

const article = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Article',
  headline: "DMARC Aggregate Reports",
  description: "DMARC aggregate reports: how to read RUA XML reports from Gmail, Microsoft. Source IPs, pass rates, dispositions.",
  inLanguage: 'en',
  author: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'PromptDNS', url: 'https://promptdns.com/' },
  publisher: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'PromptDNS', url: 'https://promptdns.com/', logo: { '@type': 'ImageObject', url: 'https://promptdns.com/favicon.svg' } },
  datePublished: '2026-10-27',
  dateModified: '2026-10-27',
};

const faqSchema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'FAQPage',
  mainEntity: [
    {'@type': 'Question', 'name': "Why do I receive multiple reports per day?", "acceptedAnswer": { '@type': 'Answer', "text": "Each mailbox provider (Gmail, Microsoft, Yahoo) sends its own report. If mail claiming to be from your domain passed through multiple providers, you receive one report from each." } },
    {'@type': 'Question', 'name': "What should I do with unknown source IPs?", "acceptedAnswer": { '@type': 'Answer', "text": "Check if the IP belongs to a service you use. If not, it may be a spoofing attempt. If your policy is p=none, the mail was delivered but flagged in the report." } },
    {'@type': 'Question', 'name': "Can I send aggregate reports to multiple addresses?", "acceptedAnswer": { '@type': 'Answer', "text": "Yes: rua accepts a comma-separated list of mailto URIs, though large providers cap the number per record. Two addresses is the common pattern." } }
  ],
};

const breadcrumbs = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
  itemListElement: [
    { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'Home', item: 'https://promptdns.com/' },
    { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: 'Email Authentication', item: 'https://promptdns.com/email-authentication/' },
    { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 3, name: "DMARC Aggregate Reports" },
  ],
};
---
<BaseLayout
  title="DMARC Aggregate Reports: How to Read RUA XML Reports from Gmail and Microsoft"
  description="DMARC aggregate reports: how to read RUA XML reports from Gmail, Microsoft. Source IPs, pass rates, dispositions."
  schema={[article, faqSchema, breadcrumbs]}
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 py-12">
    <nav class="mb-4 text-sm text-ink-faint" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/" class="hover:text-accent">Home</a>
      <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <a href="/email-authentication/" class="hover:text-accent">Email Authentication</a>
      <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <span class="text-ink-dim">DMARC Aggregate Reports</span>
    </nav>
    <h1 class="font-display text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-ink sm:text-4xl">DMARC Aggregate Reports</h1>
    <div class="pd-answer" data-vs="answer">
      <p class="text-lg text-ink-dim">DMARC aggregate reports: how to read RUA XML reports from Gmail and Microsoft. Source IPs, pass rates, dispositions.</p>
    </div>

    <section class="not-prose my-8" aria-label="Reference table">
      <div class="glass rounded-2xl p-5 shadow-lg sm:p-7 overflow-x-auto">
        <table class='pdns-table' style='width:100%'><thead><tr><th class='whitespace-nowrap'>Field in XML</th><th class='whitespace-nowrap'>What it tells you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='pd-mono'>report_metadata.org_name</td><td>Who sent the report (google.com, microsoft.com, yahoo.com)</td></tr><tr><td class='pd-mono'>report_metadata.date_range</td><td>The 24-hour reporting window</td></tr><tr><td class='pd-mono'>policy_published.domain</td><td>Your domain (confirms the report is about you)</td></tr><tr><td class='pd-mono'>record.row.source_ip</td><td>The IP address that sent email claiming to be your domain</td></tr><tr><td class='pd-mono'>record.row.count</td><td>How many messages came from this IP in this period</td></tr><tr><td class='pd-mono'>record.row.policy_evaluated.disposition</td><td>What the receiver did: none, quarantine, or reject</td></tr><tr><td class='pd-mono'>record.row.policy_evaluated.spf/dkim</td><td>Whether SPF and DKIM passed alignment for this source</td></tr><tr><td class='pd-mono'>record.identifiers.header_from</td><td>The From header domain claimed by the sender</td></tr></tbody></table>
      </div>
    </section>

    <article class="rich-text mt-10 max-w-none">
      <h2>Technical details</h2>
      <p class='mt-3'>A DMARC aggregate report is a daily XML document sent by mailbox providers to the rua= address in your DMARC record, containing a summary of all messages that claimed to be from your domain during a 24-hour period.</p><p class='mt-3'>Each record element in the XML represents a unique source IP address and includes the message count, SPF result, DKIM result, and the disposition (none, quarantine, or reject) applied by the receiving server.</p><p class='mt-3'>Aggregate reports do not contain message content: they are statistical summaries designed to help domain owners identify all legitimate sending sources and detect spoofing attempts.</p>

      <aside class="mt-8 rounded-xl border-l-3 border-l-violet/50 bg-violet/5 p-5" aria-label="Practitioner field notes">
        <p class="font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-violet mb-2">Field notes</p>
        <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim italic">The fastest way to identify a spoofing attempt: look for source IPs with high volume, failing DMARC, and a header_from that matches your domain. These are imposters. Legitimate sources you recognize should show pass rates above 90%.</p>
      </aside>

      <h2 class="font-display mt-10 text-xl font-semibold text-ink">Frequently asked questions</h2>
      <div class="mt-3 grid gap-3">
        <details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">Why do I receive multiple reports per day?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">Each mailbox provider (Gmail, Microsoft, Yahoo) sends its own report. If mail claiming to be from your domain passed through multiple providers, you receive one report from each.</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">What should I do with unknown source IPs?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">Check if the IP belongs to a service you use. If not, it may be a spoofing attempt. If your policy is p=none, the mail was delivered but flagged in the report.</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">Can I send aggregate reports to multiple addresses?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">Yes: rua accepts a comma-separated list of mailto URIs, though large providers cap the number per record. Two addresses is the common pattern.</p></details>
      </div>

      <p class="mt-8 text-xs text-ink-faint">
        Check your domain with our free tools:
        <a href="/spf-record-checker/" class="text-accent hover:text-accent-soft">SPF checker</a>,
        <a href="/dmarc-record-checker/" class="text-accent hover:text-accent-soft">DMARC checker</a>,
        <a href="/dkim-record-checker/" class="text-accent hover:text-accent-soft">DKIM checker</a>.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
